WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.000
SGIP: Learning Scene-Grounded Interaction Priors for Scene-Aware Human Motion Prediction. NeurIPS 2026.

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:15.000
The same observed motion can lead to several plausible interaction targets. SGIP makes future-motion grounding explicit.

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:23.000
The student predicts a grounding prior over object instances and a navigation-region token, then conditions motion on the selected token.

00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:28.000
During training, textual intent and semantic and geometric scores construct a privileged teacher prior.

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:33.000
Both the grounding prior and predicted motion are distilled into an observation-only student.

00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:41.000
At inference, SGIP uses observed motion and a 3D scene only. It requires no gaze, textual intent, or LLM.

00:00:41.000 --> 00:00:46.000
Kitchen comparison from the paper. SGIP is shown above gaze-free SIF3D*. Yellow: observed. Red: ground-truth future. Blue: predicted future.

00:00:46.000 --> 00:00:51.000
Living-room comparison from the paper. Compare the predicted trajectory and final interaction under the same scene.

00:00:51.000 --> 00:00:59.000
Changing the selected interaction token changes the predicted path and final pose, while keeping the observed motion, scene, and model fixed.

00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:06.000
GIMO Traj-path error is 14.5 percent lower than gaze-free GAP3DS*, 642 to 549. PROX Traj-dest error is 12.6 percent lower than gaze-free SIF3D*, 659 to 576.

00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:12.000
Ground the interaction. Predict the motion. Explore SGIP at dhsoon02.github.io/SGIP/.

